---
source: crates/leptoskit_db_macros/src/tests.rs
expression: "report.join(\"\\n\")"
---
no ends: a link names both its ends: `from = Post as tags, to = Tag as posts`
one end: a link names both its ends: `from = Post as tags, to = Tag as posts`
same columns: both ends would be the column `user_id`; name them, such as `from_column = "follower_id", to_column = "followed_id"`
declared end: `tag_id` is one of the link's ends, which `#[db::link]` declares itself; declare only the link's own columns
own key: a link's key is its two ends; it can't have another
unique: a link already holds each pair of rows at most once: its two ends are its key, so `unique` isn't needed. `exclusive` lets each `to` row be linked from one `from` row only
unknown link option: unknown link option; expected `name`, `from`, `to`, `from_column`, `to_column`, `exclusive`, `namespace`, `public`, `projection`, `index`, `check`, `hooks`, `audit`, `renamed_from`, `pack`, or `crate`
ends on a table: `from`, `to`, and `exclusive` describe a link table: use `#[db::link(...)]`
undeclared projection: `SelfUser`: declare it on the table first: `projection(...)`
secret in a projection: `SelfUser`: a `secret` column never leaves the server, so it can't be in a projection
public in a projection: `SelfUser`: a public column is in every projection already; `in(...)` names the projections a `private` column is shown in
projection twice: `SelfUser` is already one of this table's client types
projection named like the public type: `PublicUser` is already one of this table's client types
mixin field in a projection: a mixin's field can't be `in(...)` a projection: projections belong to tables
